.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-3.txt:15:   Concrete scenario: HMAC calculation embeds `key_path`, `RESTORE_PATH`, and `backup` directly inside Python source. A legitimate checkout/archive path containing `'` aborts the HMAC branch; a crafted path can terminate the literal and execute Python before the HMAC comparison. This requires a target-local backup key, but that is a supported branch. The defect is inherited from v1.3.0 and remains live in the modified uninstall flow.  
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-3.txt:18:2. **P1 — `templates/codex/pre-push-review-gate.sh:8`**  
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-3.txt:19:   Concrete scenario: the newly added manual installation command uses unconditional `cp` to `.git/hooks/pre-push`. An adopter following it silently overwrites an existing security, lint, or deployment hook with no backup or chaining. Condition 26 discloses that the gate is manual, but not this ownership loss.  
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-3.txt:20:   Minimal fix: refuse when either a file or symlink already occupies `pre-push`, and document explicit chaining or installation under a distinct hook name.
