.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-3.txt:14:1. **P1 — `scripts/uninstall.sh:247`, `:249-250`, `:551`, `:553-554`**  
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-3.txt-15-   Concrete scenario: HMAC calculation embeds `key_path`, `RESTORE_PATH`, and `backup` directly inside Python source. A legitimate checkout/archive path containing `'` aborts the HMAC branch; a crafted path can terminate the literal and execute Python before the HMAC comparison. This requires a target-local backup key, but that is a supported branch. The defect is inherited from v1.3.0 and remains live in the modified uninstall flow.  
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-3.txt-16-   Minimal fix: pass every path as a separate `sys.argv` operand to a constant Python program; never interpolate filesystem names into `python3 -c` source.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-3.txt-17-
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-3.txt:18:2. **P1 — `templates/codex/pre-push-review-gate.sh:8`**  
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-3.txt-19-   Concrete scenario: the newly added manual installation command uses unconditional `cp` to `.git/hooks/pre-push`. An adopter following it silently overwrites an existing security, lint, or deployment hook with no backup or chaining. Condition 26 discloses that the gate is manual, but not this ownership loss.  
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-3.txt:20:   Minimal fix: refuse when either a file or symlink already occupies `pre-push`, and document explicit chaining or installation under a distinct hook name.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-3.txt-21-
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-3.txt:22:3. **P1 — `templates/codex/pre-push-review-gate.sh:36-38`, `:236-238`; `templates/grok/pre-push-review-gate.sh:360-362`; `templates/.github/workflows/validate.yml.template:40`**  
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-3.txt-23-   Concrete scenario: both gates claim a server-side `validate.yml` rider rechecks `Pair-Rail-Reviewed: APPROVE`. The delivered 251-line workflow contains no trailer or review-record check. `git push --no-verify` therefore bypasses the client gate, and this workflow can remain green without cross-vendor review. CODEOWNERS does not implement the claimed trailer check.  
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-3.txt-24-   Minimal fix: remove the rider/backstop claims, or add a fail-closed workflow step that checks every canonical-touching pushed commit.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-3.txt-25-
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-3.txt:26:4. **P1 — `templates/settings/settings.user.json:185`, `:216`; rule at `AGENTS.md:9-11`**  
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-3.txt-27-   Concrete scenario: the new generated derivation asserts cold-start and latency advantages—“5 ferramentas em vez de 14 cold-starts”—despite the repository’s explicit prohibition on speed or throughput claims. Generator parity merely reproduces the prohibited claim.  
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-3.txt-28-   Minimal fix: describe only the functional matcher scope and exclusion rationale; remove the latency/cold-start language.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-3.txt-29-
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-3.txt:30:## P2 follow-ups
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-3.txt-31-
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-3.txt:32:- **P2 — `scripts/uninstall.sh:211`**: dry-run says it “would REMOVE” a tracked parent directory before checking emptiness. If adopter files remain, the real `rmdir` preserves it. Change the preview to “would attempt to remove if empty,” or evaluate projected emptiness first.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-3.txt:33:- **P2 — `templates/grok/pre-push-review-gate.sh:23`, `:171`, `:357`; `.claude/hooks/check_codex_stop_review.py:135`**: the Grok gate reads `grok-review-log.jsonl`, but the only shipped recorder writes `codex-review-log.jsonl`; the advertised sidecar route cannot clear the gate. Ship a Grok recorder or use one shared log contract.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-3.txt:34:- **P2 — `templates/.github/workflows/benchmarks.yml.template:119-122`, `:127-133`**: output names use only the benchmark basename. Two skills containing `benchmarks/regression.yaml` overwrite each other’s JSON and Markdown, leaving misleading artifacts even though the aggregate failure flag survives. Derive a collision-free name from the relative path.
