.claude/plans/PLAN-192/repass-rc1-20260918-NOGO-r2/verdict-rc1-1.txt:11:- **P2 — Inline scripts can exceed their snapshot reader’s limit.** `.claude/hooks/_lib/launch_ledger.py:267`, `:239`, `:467`, `:610` — all added by this diff. Recording accepts an inline script larger than 8 MiB, but subsequent snapshot validation rejects it through `_read_script_file`. An in-memory reproduction saved **8,388,610 bytes**, bound the launch by `tool_use_id`, then resumed with different args: the guard returned `{}` with `inconclusive / script_snapshot_missing`, despite the snapshot existing intact. **Minimal fix:** align recording and validation limits; if oversized inline scripts remain supported, validate their snapshots separately from the `scriptPath` read cap.
