.claude/plans/PLAN-192/repass-rc1-20260918-NOGO-r2/verdict-rc1-3.txt-8-   [`.claude/scripts/approval_gate.py:215`](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc1.3JOeTU/wt/.claude/scripts/approval_gate.py:215). Evidence containing `"findings":[{"severity":"P0"}],"findings":[]` passes: `json.load` silently retains the second value. With otherwise valid evidence, the CLI returned **rc 0, APPROVED, empty reasons**. This differs from the declared NaN and unknown-policy-key defects.  
.claude/plans/PLAN-192/repass-rc1-20260918-NOGO-r2/verdict-rc1-3.txt-9-   **Minimal fix:** reject duplicate object keys, including nested keys, through an `object_pairs_hook`; return the existing input-rejection result.
.claude/plans/PLAN-192/repass-rc1-20260918-NOGO-r2/verdict-rc1-3.txt-10-
.claude/plans/PLAN-192/repass-rc1-20260918-NOGO-r2/verdict-rc1-3.txt:11:2. **P1 annex — An incomplete test scan turns ambiguity into accepted proof.**  
.claude/plans/PLAN-192/repass-rc1-20260918-NOGO-r2/verdict-rc1-3.txt-12-   [`.claude/scripts/test_refs.py:59`](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc1.3JOeTU/wt/.claude/scripts/test_refs.py:59). Two files defining `test_shared` correctly produce rc 3. Injecting `PermissionError` when reading one file instead makes `match` accept the bare declaration against the other file’s explicit node, returning **rc 0 with no errors**. Unreadability is silently treated as absence.  
.claude/plans/PLAN-192/repass-rc1-20260918-NOGO-r2/verdict-rc1-3.txt-13-   **Minimal fix:** preserve scan failures and refuse resolution requiring repository-wide uniqueness when the scan is incomplete.
.claude/plans/PLAN-192/repass-rc1-20260918-NOGO-r2/verdict-rc1-3.txt-14-
.claude/plans/PLAN-192/repass-rc1-20260918-NOGO-r2/verdict-rc1-3.txt:15:3. **P1 annex — Mutation-command timeouts leave descendants running.**  
.claude/plans/PLAN-192/repass-rc1-20260918-NOGO-r2/verdict-rc1-3.txt-16-   [`.claude/scripts/mutant_sandbox.py:133`](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc1.3JOeTU/wt/.claude/scripts/mutant_sandbox.py:133), [cleanup at :147](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc1.3JOeTU/wt/.claude/scripts/mutant_sandbox.py:147). When a test command launches workers, `subprocess.run(timeout=…)` kills its direct child without terminating the descendants. A read-only process probe reproduced a surviving descendant after timeout. The helper then removes the worktree beneath those processes; repeated retries can accumulate workers and interfere with subsequent verification.  
.claude/plans/PLAN-192/repass-rc1-20260918-NOGO-r2/verdict-rc1-3.txt-17-   **Minimal fix:** isolate command execution in a process group and terminate/wait for its descendants before removing the sandbox.
.claude/plans/PLAN-192/repass-rc1-20260918-NOGO-r2/verdict-rc1-3.txt-18-
.claude/plans/PLAN-192/repass-rc1-20260918-NOGO-r2/verdict-rc1-3.txt:19:**P2 follow-ups**
.claude/plans/PLAN-192/repass-rc1-20260918-NOGO-r2/verdict-rc1-3.txt-20-
.claude/plans/PLAN-192/repass-rc1-20260918-NOGO-r2/verdict-rc1-3.txt-21-- **Successful `relaunch --out` without a copy.** [`.claude/scripts/ceo-launches.py:186`](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc1.3JOeTU/wt/.claude/scripts/ceo-launches.py:186). After the initial integrity check succeeds, the snapshot is read again. Making this second read unavailable produced **rc 0**, an “exact recorded call” heading, and no output file. **Minimal fix:** validate and consume one snapshot buffer; otherwise return nonzero before announcing an exact call.
