.claude/plans/PLAN-192/repass-rc1-20260918-NOGO-r1/verdict-rc1-1.txt-2-
.claude/plans/PLAN-192/repass-rc1-20260918-NOGO-r1/verdict-rc1-1.txt:3:1. **P1 — Condition 10 false: incomplete index reads can block legitimate resumes.** [`.claude/hooks/_lib/launch_ledger.py:487`](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc1.Eh6UQ9/wt/.claude/hooks/_lib/launch_ledger.py:487) returns the accumulated prefix after an `OSError`. Suppose a run launched with args A, then deliberately resumed and bound with args B. If the next index read fails before B’s binding, a legitimate resume with B is compared against A and blocked. I reproduced `mismatch_blocked`; a torn newest binding produces the same stale comparison. **Minimal fix:** expose index-read integrity to guard lookup; incomplete history must produce `inconclusive` and a breadcrumb, never authoritative older evidence.
.claude/plans/PLAN-192/repass-rc1-20260918-NOGO-r1/verdict-rc1-1.txt-4-
.claude/plans/PLAN-192/repass-rc1-20260918-NOGO-r1/verdict-rc1-1.txt:5:2. **P1 — Condition 7 false: ambiguous response IDs receive strong bindings.** [`.claude/hooks/_lib/launch_ledger.py:315`](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc1.Eh6UQ9/wt/.claude/hooks/_lib/launch_ledger.py:315) immediately accepts the first structured key. For `{"runId":"wf_11111111-aa","run_id":"wf_22222222-bb"}`, PostToolUse binds the first ID as `by_tool_use`, despite the ambiguity. Separately, the regex at [line 110](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc1.Eh6UQ9/wt/.claude/hooks/_lib/launch_ledger.py:110) extracts `wf_12345678` from `Run ID: wf_12345678-123456789`, inventing a shortened identity. Either can associate subsequent comparisons with the wrong run. **Minimal fix:** require agreement between structured ID fields and validate complete tokens without accepting malformed prefixes.
.claude/plans/PLAN-192/repass-rc1-20260918-NOGO-r1/verdict-rc1-1.txt-6-
.claude/plans/PLAN-192/repass-rc1-20260918-NOGO-r1/verdict-rc1-1.txt:7:3. **P1 — Condition 12 false: `no_manifest` is silent.** [`.claude/hooks/_lib/launch_ledger.py:791`](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc1.Eh6UQ9/wt/.claude/hooks/_lib/launch_ledger.py:791) records `no_manifest` and returns `{}`; the wrapper emits no warning for it. Resuming from another worktree—or resuming a run launched before upgrading from v1.4.0—therefore proceeds without the promised “só aviso.” **Minimal fix:** return an explicit notice that the call proceeds without a recorded baseline.
