.claude/plans/PLAN-192/repass-rc1-20260918-NOGO-r1/verdict-rc1-1.txt:11:4. **P1 — The advisory recovery route returns the changed inputs.** [`.claude/hooks/_lib/launch_ledger.py:757`](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc1.Eh6UQ9/wt/.claude/hooks/_lib/launch_ledger.py:757) identifies the current launch as the recorded call and recommends `relaunch <run-id>`. Reproduction: launch A; allow accidental args B in advisory mode; PostToolUse binds B; follow the recovery command. It prints **B**, with an “exact recorded call” heading. This is particularly easy to miss when reviewing PreToolUse and PostToolUse separately. **Minimal fix:** reference the immutable `against` launch ID and the existing `show <against>` command; any relaunch recovery route must likewise select that specific launch.
