.claude/plans/PLAN-192/repass-ga/verdict-ga-1.txt

Fresh installs that create settings activate the hook immediately; qualifying upgrades register it through settings merge. Existing settings survive a fresh installation unchanged. Runs launched before upgrading have no baseline and resume silently, as condition **12** declares.
Two declared P1 risks deserve emphasis because they are reachable on these installation paths. All cited lines are additions in the supplied diff:
- **P1 — Signed known-open: stale bindings can block legitimate resumes.** [`.claude/hooks/_lib/launch_ledger.py:487`](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-ga.fxIjzL/wt/.claude/hooks/_lib/launch_ledger.py:487) and [line 640](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-ga.fxIjzL/wt/.claude/hooks/_lib/launch_ledger.py:640). After intentionally changing A → B, a torn latest binding or failed binding append leaves A authoritative. Probes reproduced B being blocked; the append-failure probe also accepted A as `match`. Declared by condition **10** and the incorporated round-3 annex. **Minimal fix:** make incomplete history and uncommitted newer resumes inconclusive instead of trusting the older baseline.
- **P1 — Signed known-open: script copying precedes permission approval.** [`.claude/hooks/_lib/launch_ledger.py:274`](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-ga.fxIjzL/wt/.claude/hooks/_lib/launch_ledger.py:274) and [line 420](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-ga.fxIjzL/wt/.claude/hooks/_lib/launch_ledger.py:420). A denied source can acquire a readable copy in project state; copying occurs even when this guard itself blocks. Condition **23** accurately discloses this. Advisory mode retains the copying. **Minimal fix:** defer dereferencing and snapshotting until authorization is established.

